Covers the doc-driven investigation that revealed (a) Anthropic
deprecated thinking.budget_tokens for Opus 4.7+ (so patch 1 was
handling the wrong field), (b) Claude Code only emits output_config.effort
when the model is recognized as supporting it (needed the
_SUPPORTED_CAPABILITIES env var), and (c) modelOverrides doesn't apply
to LLM-gateway paths so model translation must happen proxy-side.

Documents the wrapper env-var stack:
  ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7[1m]
  ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL_SUPPORTED_CAPABILITIES=effort,xhigh_effort,...
  CLAUDE_AUTOCOMPACT_PCT_OVERRIDE=80
  --model opus

Includes the end-to-end wire-format verification dump showing
output_config.effort:xhigh → reasoning_effort:xhigh translation
working, with claude-opus-4-7 → claude-opus-4.7-1m-internal upstream.
